powerpcspe: *frob_tf_ti must not overlap its input

*frob_tf_ti moves a TImode value held in four 32-bit GPRs into TFmode,
two 64-bit GPRs, with two evmergelo.  The output had no earlyclobber,
so the register allocator could put it on top of the input: for TI in
r6..r9 and TF in r8..r9 the first evmergelo writes r8 before the second
one reads it, and the low double of an IBM long double comes out as a
copy of a word of the high one.  Seen after __gcc_qdiv returns with
-mlong-double-128 -O2 on e500v2; every long double result passing
through TImode can be hit.  *frob_ti_tf, the opposite direction,
already has "=&r".

--- gcc-8.5.0.orig/gcc/config/powerpcspe/spe.md	2026-11-27 14:59:30.928968199 +0100
+++ gcc-8.5.0/gcc/config/powerpcspe/spe.md	2026-11-27 14:59:31.109972837 +0100
@@ -2314,7 +2314,7 @@
 })
 
 (define_insn "*frob_tf_ti"
-  [(set (match_operand:TF 0 "gpc_reg_operand" "=r")
+  [(set (match_operand:TF 0 "gpc_reg_operand" "=&r")
         (subreg:TF (match_operand:TI 1 "gpc_reg_operand" "r") 0))]
   "TARGET_E500_DOUBLE"
 {
